.TH AVR\-REPO\-CLONE 1 "" "avr 0.2.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-repo-clone \- Clone a repository from its nearest available Avrea mirror.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr repo clone
[OPTIONS] REPOSITORY [DIRECTORY]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Clone a repository from its nearest available Avrea mirror.
.PP
REPOSITORY is an owner/repository name or an Avrea repository ID (rep-...). Available placements are raced from this client; the first to serve the repository wins. Use --placement to select an exact URL or hostname.
.PP
The origin remote stays on the selected mirror. A repository-local Avrea credential helper obtains fresh Git JWTs for subsequent fetch, pull, and push operations using your Avrea login. Tokens normally last one hour; scoped API keys have a shorter server-enforced lifetime. Tokens are never saved in the repository. Pushes require server-side write permission.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr repo clone foo/faa
    avr repo clone foo/faa my-checkout --depth 1
    avr repo clone foo/faa --placement https://git.fi.a.avrea.io
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIREPOSITORY\fR
\&
.TP
[\fIDIRECTORY\fR]
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-placement\fR \fITEXT\fR
Exact mirror URL or hostname from the repository's placements.
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses the default organization if omitted.
.TP
\fB\-\-branch\fR, \fB\-b\fR \fITEXT\fR
Branch or tag to check out.
.TP
\fB\-\-depth\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Create a shallow clone with this many commits.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-repo (1),
.BR avr-repo-list (1),
.BR avr-repo-mirror (1),
.BR avr-repo-public-mirror (1)
